<title>GERMANY: German September trade surplus rises to 8.3 bln DM.</title>
<headline>German September trade surplus rises to 8.3 bln DM.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator (bln marks):</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC Sept 96   Aug 96	 Sept 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		 +8.3     +8.1	    +7.6</p>
<p> Current account	     -1.6     -4.6	    -2.4</p>
<p> Exports			 64.0     58.4	    63.8</p>
<p> Imports			 55.7     50.3	    56.2</p>
<p> Services			-6.0     -5.7	    -4.8</p>
<p> Wage and property income  -2.9     -0.8	    -0.7</p>
<p> Transfers		     -1.1     -5.9	    -4.9</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	 +0.1     -0.3	    +0.4</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC Jan-Sept 96     Jan-Sept 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		  +69.1	     +61.2</p>
<p> Current account		-23.0	     -21.0</p>
<p> Exports			  573.2	     553.4</p>
<p> Imports			  504.1	     492.2</p>
<p> Services			 -42.6	     -43.9</p>
<p> Wage and property income    -8.9		+3.9</p>
<p> Transfers			-38.6	     -40.4</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	   -2.0		-1.8</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
